===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.|en}} '''[[polaris|polāris]]'''

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpəʊ̯lə(ɹ)/|[ˈpʰəʊ̯lə(ɹ)]|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpoʊ̯lɚ/|[ˈpʰoʊ̯lɚ]|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊlə(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of, relating to, measured from, or referred to a [[geographic]] [[pole]] (the [[North Pole]] or [[South Pole]]).
# {{lb|en|space sciences}} Of an [[orbit]] that passes over, or near, one of these poles.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Having a [[dipole]]; [[ionic]].
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Of a [[coordinate]] [[system]], specifying the [[location]] of a [[point]] in a [[plane]] by using a [[radius]] and an [[angle]].
# {{lb|en|linguistics|of a [[question]]}} Having but [[two]] possible [[answer]]s, ''[[yes]]'' and ''[[no]]''.

